From 8ace97d799e544b9c1db848b7bafb10d52381b70 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Naveen Sivasamy <naves@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Mon, 30 Mar 2026 14:54:36 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] UPSTREAM:PROTOCOL:sigma_dut: Fix uninitialized addr buffer
 breaking MAC address retry logic

The retry logic in fetch_ap_mac_address_nl() determines whether a MAC
address fetch failed by checking if the addr buffer is all zeros. If
so, it retries up to FETCH_MAC_ADDRESS_MAX_RETRIES times to handle the
interface initialization delay on split-PHY RDPs.

Callers may pass uninitialized stack buffers to this function, leaving
them with indeterminate (non-zero) values. As a result, the zero-check
never triggers, retries never occur, and an invalid MAC address is
silently returned to the caller.

Add a memset to zero-initialize the addr buffer at the start of
fetch_ap_mac_address_nl() to ensure the retry condition fires
correctly regardless of the caller's buffer state.

Patch-dependency: 113-UPSTREAM-PROTOCOL-sigma_dut-Add-retry-logic-for-fetc.patch
Fixes: I5ff5ed495 (UPSTREAM:PROTOCOL:sigma_dut: Add retry logic for
fetching MAC address and fix get_interface_handler crashes)

Signed-off-by: Naveen Sivasamy <naves@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
 ap.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

--- a/ap.c
+++ b/ap.c
@@ -16141,6 +16141,7 @@ static int fetch_ap_mac_address_nl(struc
 	struct get_mac_addr_info arg;
 	int iter;

+	memset(addr, 0, ETH_ALEN);
 	arg.ifname = (char *)ifname;
 	arg.attr = attr;
 	arg.value = value;
